      <title>China’s Spies Set Sights on A.I. Chips Years Before Nvidia Scandal</title>
      <link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/21/world/asia/china-nvidia-spy-chips-state-security.html</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/21/world/asia/china-nvidia-spy-chips-state-security.html</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 04:28:43 +0000</pubDate>
      <enclosure url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/22/multimedia/22int-china-mss-01-bjfp/22int-china-mss-01-bjfp-mediumSquareAt3X-v2.jpg" length="0" type="image/jpeg" />
      <media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/22/multimedia/22int-china-mss-01-bjfp/22int-china-mss-01-bjfp-mediumSquareAt3X-v2.jpg" medium="image" />
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/22/multimedia/22int-china-mss-01-bjfp/22int-china-mss-01-bjfp-mediumSquareAt3X-v2.jpg" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;margin-bottom:10px;" alt="China’s Spies Set Sights on A.I. Chips Years Before Nvidia Scandal" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;China’s espionage agency has been running a secret campaign to help the country’s companies acquire advanced A.I. chips and to gather intelligence on the sector, officials say.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
