      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/22/multimedia/22int-cartel-ticktock-photo1-bpwm/22int-cartel-ticktock-photo1-bpwm-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;margin-bottom:10px;" alt="Drones, Texts and Diversions: How Mexico Captured a Most Wanted Man" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;U.S. and Mexican authorities shared intelligence for weeks to track Fausto Isidro Meza Flores, a drug cartel leader that a U.S. official called the most dangerous man in Mexico.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
